  "description": "Fast arbitrary-precision integers for .NET: an alternative to System.Numerics.BigInteger with the same API (operators, Parse / ToString, bytes, generic math). Hand-written assembly kernels (x64, x86, ARM64, ARMv7) and sub-quadratic algorithms make it faster than BigInteger at every size on x64 (on ARM64 on par at a few words; on 32-bit ARM from 8-32 words): 1.1-5x on numbers of a few words, 10-100x on large ones (against .NET 10; multiplication, division, decimal conversion). The same kernels in the C++ version run on par with GMP on x64 and x86. No native dependencies to install; a managed core runs on every other platform.",
  "id": "FullInt",
  "isPrerelease": true,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-28T01:52:33.09Z",
